<title>POLAND: FORECAST - Polish August y/y CPI seen at 13.7 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Polish August y/y CPI seen at 13.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer prices and unemployment are expected to fall faster than assumed in official predictions with year-on-year inflation dipping below 14 percent in August, Tadeusz Chroscicki, chief analyst at the government's Centre for Strategic Studies (CSS) said.</p>
<p>He said in his macroeconomic short-term forecast submitted monthly to Reuters that also industrial and construction output should show robust growth along with investment.</p>
<p>Chroscicki said the main negative factor for the economy was a continuation of strong imports, which far outpace growth in exports and resulted in a fast widening trade deficit. @</p>
